92
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:13,860
I assure you, it is.

93
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,340
She's way out of my league.

94
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,140
My sister?

95
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,160
We're still talking about the same person, right?

96
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:22,900
I know exactly what you're thinking, so you can stop looking at me like that, okay?

97
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:23,480
Huh?

98
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,780
Please excuse her for the time being.

99
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:28,500
Totally fine.

100
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:30,200
I'm just happy I ran into you.

101
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:33,760
Talking with you outside of school is kind of like a dream come true.

102
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:36,820
Oh, I shouldn't have said that.

103
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:38,720
Ishikawa would get upset if he knew.

104
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:43,240
You're sweet, which is why I don't think he'd mind at all.

105
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:52,700
I know for a fact, Toadu wouldn't be upset.

106
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:55,880
But I keep on lying.

107
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,200
Guess what?

108
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:01,660
I heard they're dating now.

109
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:03,880
Aw, it makes sense, though.

110
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:04,800
Think about it.

111
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,100
They're constantly together.

112
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:07,200
Oh, for sure.

113
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:14,260
They make such a good couple.

114
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,860
I know that we've got Kono completely fooled.

115
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:27,380
Fooled how?

116
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:31,560
She thinks I'm dating Toadu, right?

117
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,280
She actually fell for a charade.

118
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,520
I have no clue.

119
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:38,320
She hasn't mentioned it to me.

120
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:39,740
She did.

121
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:41,960
Because she asked about it yesterday.

122
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,040
And I didn't deny it.

123
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:45,860
I said the rumors were true.

124
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,780
Why did I say that, though?

125
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:51,260
What part of me thought I would be okay to light her face?

126
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:56,140
And you're telling me this because you're hoping I'll explain to Sakura what's really going on.

127
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:57,240
Mm-hmm.

128
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:00,160
Remy doesn't have to explain, you know.

129
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:02,700
If you really do have a crush on him, I'll stay quiet.

130
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,900
That's not fair.

131
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:07,180
I'm failing to see how.

132
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:13,060
What's unfair is you, Yuki.

133
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:16,860
She's right.

134
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:19,200
I'm not being considerate of Kono.

135
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:20,400
At all.

136
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:24,140
I was well aware lying would hurt her.

137
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,000
But I did it anyway.

138
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:30,040
I'm terrible.

139
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:41,320
As she was running away, I saw her lips trembling so fast.

140
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:42,700
I didn't know they could do that.

141
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:45,280
All right, then.

142
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,940
It's about time I started telling the truth.

143
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:49,540
So here it is.

144
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,760
I see.

145
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,600
Thanks for being honest, Yuki.

146
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:06,000
I know this won't last forever.

147
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,560
I knew it from the very beginning.

148
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:12,140
Toru would have to have romantic feelings for me.

149
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:13,540
And he doesn't.

150
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:18,420
The first day we pretended to be dating should have also been the last.

151
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:22,560
But he still holds my hand.

152
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:29,100
He's so nice to me, even when I don't deserve it.

153
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:33,280
We might have to keep this up, just in case he catches on.

154
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,060
Are you okay with that?

155
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:39,680
Yeah, sure.

156
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:40,640
It's fine.

157
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:48,040
Being found out didn't really bother me.

158
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:51,980
I think what I wanted was for our lie to become something real.

159
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:57,980
But, even if it did, it would always be tainted.

160
00:08:57,980 --> 00:09:06,060
Ah, Yuki was absent yet again.

161
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:08,560
Jeez, how many days is that?

162
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:09,680
Three, I think.

163
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:10,560
Or four.

164
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:13,320
However long it's been, I don't like it one bit.

165
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,280
I wonder if maybe she's sick.

166
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:18,360
Being sick wouldn't stop her from returning my texts, though.

167
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:20,020
Have you heard from her?

168
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:22,060
Toru?

169
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:23,760
Oh, sorry.

170
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:24,440
